  // Teaches: the blob deforms. This is the one level that could not exist
  // with rigid bodies — the gap under the wall is 30 units and the blob is
  // 45 across, so it has to be squashed through, and there is no way to
  // rotate or wedge a rigid object past that.
  //
  // The blob's pressure is 0.9 rather than 1.05: an under-inflated body
  // gives way more readily, and a level whose whole point is deformation
  // should not also be a level about shoving very hard.

